IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 593 of 2007
CITATION: (2011) 1 SCC 609
YEAR: 2011

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.K. Jain, P. Sathasivam, J.M. Panchal, R.M. Lodha, H.L. Dattu

PARTIES:
Vijaysinh Chandubha Jadeja vs State of Gujarat

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1985

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 50 NDPS

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
personal search, gazetted officer, magistrate option, mandatory compliance

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Constitution bench held that informing suspect of their statutory right under Section 50 NDPS to be searched before a Gazetted Officer or Magistrate is mandatory; failure vitiates conviction.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 50 NDPS.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

